meta {
  name: (7-1) Search for person in CET
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{domain}}/tree/search?q.givenName=William&q.surname=Heaton&f.treeId={{treeId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  q.givenName: William
  q.surname: Heaton
  f.treeId: {{treeId}}
}

docs {
  In order to search just a specific CET tree, the request must include a facet identifying which tree to search in the query parameters. This example shows setting f.treeId to the tree ID we created in step 2 in order to find our personId1 object.
  
  If the status code from this request is 200 OK, proceed to (8-1) GET Matches.
}
